{"_v":1,"id":"the-robber-bridegroom-1976","bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"/people/Ben-Brantley/","q":"But every so often, the score and the staging melt into a quieter, creepier form of enchantment that summons some of the shimmering mystery of Welty's book."},{"cn":"Jesse Green","o":"Vulture","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"/people/Jesse-Green/","q":"Timbers draws from his usual bag of magic tricks, prop jokes, unexpected taxidermy, and winking meta-theatricality to keep the eye and attention engaged at all times. Even so, the story, having been pulled away from any real engagement with its dark fundamentals, now seems like an excuse instead of the point."},{"cn":"Robert Hofler","o":"TheWrap","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://news.google.com/news/url?sr=1&sa=t&ct2=us%2F0_0_s_6_0_t&usg=AFQjCNFS17MsKKQ-cp8x7Oid99NaA9MFPg&did=9cbf494182487077&cid=52779062333295&ei=98XmVrDjLYrA3AHVi724Dw&rt=STORY&vm=STANDARD&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.thewrap.com%2Fthe-robber-bridegroom-theater-review-steven-pasquale-soars-but-show-is-more-hee-haw-than-southern%2F","q":"Pasquale brings his easy, natural charm to the stage."}],"au":{"score":83,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":83,"c":7,"sr":4.1}}},"pd":"1976-09-28","ca":[{"n":"Barry Bostwick","r":"Jamie Lockhart"},{"n":"Rhonda Coullet","r":"Rosamund"},{"n":"Barbara Lang","r":"Salome"},{"n":"Susan Berger","r":"Goat's Mother"},{"n":"George Deloy","r":"Kyle Nunnery"},{"n":"Gary Epp","r":"Harmon Harper"},{"n":"B. J. Hardin","r":"Norman Ogelsby"},{"n":"Carolyn McCurry","r":"A Raven"},{"n":"Lawrence John Moss","r":"Little Harp"},{"n":"Mary Murray","r":"Queenie Brenner"},{"n":"Trip Plymale","r":"Goat"},{"n":"Ernie Sabella","r":"Big Harp"},{"n":"Jana Schneider","r":"Airie"},{"n":"Melinda Tanner","r":"Rose Otto"},{"n":"Stephen Vinovich","r":"Clemment Musgrove"},{"n":"Dennis Warning","r":"Gerry G. Summers"},{"n":"Tom Westerman","r":"K. K. Pone"}]